WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.050
When a car turns

c2
00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:01.950
a corner,

c3
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.125
its outer wheels have

c4
00:00:03.125 --> 00:00:04.225
to travel a longer

c5
00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:05.325
path than the inner

c6
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:06.125
wheels do.

c7
00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:07.200
So the two wheels

c8
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.425
must spin at different

c9
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:09.175
speeds,

c10
00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.350
and the differential makes

c11
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.250
that possible.

c12
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.325
The engine turns a

c13
00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:13.325
ring gear and its

c14
00:00:13.325 --> 00:00:14.075
carrier,

c15
00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:15.475
and small planet gears

c16
00:00:15.475 --> 00:00:16.575
inside link the two

c17
00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:17.325
axles.

c18
00:00:17.325 --> 00:00:18.225
On a curve,

c19
00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:19.425
the planet gears start

c20
00:00:19.425 --> 00:00:20.225
to turn,

c21
00:00:20.225 --> 00:00:21.500
so one wheel speeds

c22
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.450
up while the other

c23
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.300
slows down.

c24
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.525
And through it all,

c25
00:00:24.525 --> 00:00:26.075
the carrier always moves

c26
00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:27.325
at exactly the average

c27
00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:28.100
speed of the two

c28
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:28.475
wheels.

